ync-GKR's test-only dense reference for a two-layer mixed circuit of width 4096. Direct depth-24 fresh/prepared measurements show 3.46-4.45-fold lower per-request proving-path latency. CPU and full-proof delivery studies distinguish useful parallel work from queueing and return-path costs, retaining all outcomes and latency budgets. The evaluation supports larger circuits within finite RAM, lower repeated-request cost, and explicit deployment choices for this artifact. It preserves the cryptographic claim boundary of the existing construction.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nrust/library/alloc/src/vec/spec_from_iter.rs at main · rust-lang/rust · GitHub (https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/main/library/alloc/src/vec/spec_from_iter.rs)\nciteturn1search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; use super::{IntoIter, SpecExtend, SpecFromIterNested, Vec}; ... fn from_iter(iterator: IntoIter<T>) -> Self { ... vec.spec_extend(iterator);\n\n# spec_from_iter.rs\n\n# spec_from_iter.rs\n\n## File metadata and controls\n\n  * Code\n\n  * Blame\n\n65 lines (60 loc) · 2.32 KB\n\nRaw\n\nuse core::mem::ManuallyDrop;\n\nuse core::ptr;\n\nuse super::{IntoIter, SpecExtend, SpecFromIterNested, Vec};\n\n/// Specialization trait used for Vec::from_iter\n\n///\n\n/// ## The delegation graph:\n\n///\n\n/// ```text\n\n/// +-------------+\n\n/// |FromIterator |\n\n/// +-+-----------+\n\n/// |\n\n/// v\n\n/// +-+---------------------------------+ +---------------------+\n\n/// |SpecFromIter +---->+SpecFromIterNested |\n\n/// |where I: | | |where I: |\n\n/// | Iterator (default)------------+ | | Iterator (default) |\n\n/// | vec::IntoIter | | | TrustedLen |\n\n/// | InPlaceCollect--(fallback to)-+ | +---------------------+\n\n/// +-----------------------------------+\n\n/// ```\n\npub(super) trait SpecFromIter<T, I> {\n\nfn from_iter(iter: I) -> Self;\n\n}\n\nimpl<T, I> SpecFromIter<T, I> for Vec<T>\n\nwhere\n\nI: Iterator<Item = T>,\n\n{\n\ndefault fn from_iter(iterator: I) -> Self {\n\nSpecFromIterNested::from_iter(iterator)\n\n}\n\n}\n\nimpl<T> SpecFromIter<T, IntoIter<T>> for Vec<T> {\n\nfn from_iter(iterator: IntoIter<T>) -> Self {\n\n// A common case is passing a vector into a function which immediately\n\n// re-collects into a vector. We can short circuit this if the IntoIter\n\n// has not been advanced at all.\n\n// When it has been advanced We can also reuse the memory and move the data to the front.\n\n// But we only do so when the resulting Vec wouldn't have more unused capacity\n\n// than creating it through the generic FromIterator implementation would. That limitation\n\n// is not strictly necessary as Vec's allocation behavior is intentionally unspecified.\n\n// But it is a conservative choice.\n\nlet has_advanced = iterator.buf != iterator.ptr;\n\nif !has_advanced || iterator.len() >= iterator.cap / 2 {\n\nlet it = ManuallyDrop::new(iterator);\n\n// ignore-tidy-undocumented-unsafe\n\nunsafe {\n\nif has_advanced {\n\nptr::copy(it.ptr.as_ptr(), it.buf.as_ptr(), it.len());\n\n}\n\nreturn Vec::from_parts(it.buf, it.len(), it.cap);\n\n}\n\n}\n\nlet mut vec = Vec::new();\n\n// must delegate to spec_extend() since extend() itself delegates\n\n// to spec_from for empty Vecs\n\nvec.spec_extend(iterator);\n\nvec\n\n}\n\n}--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nfix: add missing sumcheck C API functions for extension fields · ingonyama-zk/icicle@b4baff1 · GitHub (https://github.com/ingonyama-zk/icicle/actions/runs/23939657405)\nciteturn1search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; Crawled: last month; ingonyama-zk / icicle Public ... # fix: add missing sumcheck C API functions for extension fields #1013 ... Actions will be forced to run with Node.js 24 by default starting June 2nd, 2026. ... For more information see: https://github.blog/changelog/2025-09-19-deprecation-of-node-20-on-github-actions-runners/ [Button: Show more] [Button: Show less]\n\ningon